{{also|Marzipan}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|de|Marzipan}}, from {{cog|it|marzapane}}. The German ''-i-'' is probably due to a reinterpretation as {{cog|la|{{m|la|Marci}} {{m|la|panis}}||Mark's bread}}. Further origin uncertain, but now thought to be derived from {{w|Mottama|Martaban}} ({{m|my|မုတ္ထမ}}), a Burmese port known for its spice exports.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|AU|NZ}} {{IPA|/ˈmɑːzɪpæn/|/ˈmɑːzəpæn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US|CA}} {{IPA|/ˈmɑːɹzəpæn/|/ˈmɑːɹtsəpɑːn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[confection]] of [[almond]] [[paste]], [[sugar]] and [[egg white]].

